@@ -0,0 +1,99 @@
+# Paid access rollout gates
+
+The local provider-spend machinery is described in [the expenditure runbook](ai-provider-spend.md).
+It is disabled without explicit valid configuration and approved cumulative
+allowances. Unknown outcomes retain money and concurrency slots; review that
+runbook's reconciliation/availability boundary before enabling it. This local
+implementation does not resolve the anonymous-owner/shared-quota gates below.
+
+This is a preparation runbook, not a record of a live inventory, restore drill,
+deployment, purchase, or release decision. The intended iPhone purchase and paid
+use path remains account optional (D1=B). A desktop account is required for paid
+desktop access. The independent anonymous-owner proof and cross-device recovery
+contract remain to be designed and verified; a copied receipt or the mutable
+`DeviceUuid` field cannot establish ownership.
+
+## Inventory before a data or authorization change
+
+Verify the deployed API version and schema, obtain approved read-only database
+access, and run [the aggregate inventory](../ops/audit-subscription-state.sql)
+on each separate environment. Use the deployed server's trusted Apple environment
+and allowed product IDs, not client headers. For example, in an authorized
+read-only `psql` session for a Production deployment:
+
+```sql
+BEGIN READ ONLY;
+SET LOCAL owl.audit.expected_environment = 'Production';
+SET LOCAL owl.audit.allowed_product_ids = 'com.flashcardai.owlai.premium.monthly,com.flashcardai.owlai.premium.yearly';
+\i ops/audit-subscription-state.sql
+ROLLBACK;
+```
+
+Use `Sandbox` in the separate Sandbox deployment. This report emits fixed
+environment buckets and aggregate counts only. `claimed` means both
+`OwnerAccountId` and `ClaimedAt` exist; `unclaimed` means neither exists;
+`tombstoned` means the claim timestamp remains after owner deletion;
+`inconsistent_claim` means an owner exists without a claim timestamp.
+`orphan_owner` means an owner reference has no matching user. Counts of duplicate
+legacy `DeviceUuid` references and groups with several claimed accounts are
+triage signals, not proof of an anonymous owner conflict. Reason counts overlap:
+wrong environment/product, blank original ID, null expiry, PostgreSQL infinity,
+and finite expiry outside the .NET date range can coexist on one row.
+`policy_applicable_rows` mirrors the persisted-row environment, product,
+original-ID and expiry checks; it is not a count of active paid subscribers.
+
+The local synthetic test covers the report, including empty data, invalid
+settings, repeat execution in a read-only transaction, and Unicode whitespace.
+No live data has been inventoried. A real run also requires a verified backup
+and restore on a copy, old-schema migration testing through actual API startup,
+and a private reconciliation register with controlled access. Do not put raw
+transaction IDs, receipts, account IDs, or personal text in the aggregate report.
+
+## Reconciliation before enforcement
+
+The current Task4 rule quarantines existing rows whose stored environment,
+product or expiry fail trusted policy, even when a fresh Apple response is valid.
+This preserves `WasEverPaid`, ownership, tombstones and raw metadata. Resolve
+each legitimate affected purchase from independently verified Apple history and
+preserved ownership evidence. Prove that any repair is precise, repeatable,
+logged and non-destructive on a restored copy; do not require repurchase or
+erase quarantine rows as a shortcut. Preserve already claimed owners. A legacy
+unclaimed purchase needs a verified recovery route before stricter ownership
+enforcement. If live Production has no such rows, record that result and avoid
+unneeded legacy handling. If it has them, close the individual or automated
+routes before switching. No anonymous-owner table or additive migration exists
+in this bounded preparation; its design and old-data startup test are pending.
+
+## Separate environments and client distribution
+
+Run Production and Sandbox/App Review as separate API deployments, databases,
+credentials, usage counters and AI budgets. Both use
+`ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production` (or another non-Development host) and
+`TestMode__Enabled=false`. The Apple purchase environment is a separate setting:
+Production deployment trusts `Production`; the Sandbox deployment trusts
+`Sandbox`. Both require genuine Apple signatures, App Attest/request proof and
+positive quotas. `TestMode=true` is Development only; it is not an App Review
+route. Never switch a shared database from Sandbox to Production.
+
+Determine and verify how the actual TestFlight/submission build reaches the
+Sandbox backend on a physical device. Current checked-in iOS Debug and Release
+URLs point to the Production hostname, so a changed Debug URL or untrusted
+client header is insufficient. Verify StoreKit purchase, renewal, refund,
+restore and entitlement isolation on that route. Sandbox data must never grant
+Production rights. Document the final distribution mapping before submission.
+
+Deploy compatible backend contracts and a global AI spend guard before new
+clients; then release iOS and Windows and verify legacy transitions. Only after
+the anonymous-owner proof and optional desktop linking protocol are settled
+should stricter ownership enforcement be enabled. Numeric D2 AI quotas and
+money budgets remain unapproved. Existing example numbers and synthetic test
+values are not release authorization. Validate provider-attempt counters and a
+safe server-side kill switch for *new* AI calls. On failure, stop new AI spend
+without restoring vulnerable authorization or dropping purchase/claim records.
+
+The current backend `api-ci-cd.yml` manual workflow publishes images and
+deploys; it is not a test-only validation route. A separate safe test route
+or revised workflow and explicit release decision are required before remote
+validation or deployment. Task1 ownership regressions and the B4 global guest
+case remain unresolved gates. Do not infer release readiness from this local
+inventory or a health check.
